  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Ratel Lumina",
      "text": "English · [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@ratel-works/dsh-lumina) [](LICENSE)\n\n**Make development more fun.**\n\nRatel Lumina is a visual and motion enhancement plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness), available on desktop and Web / PWA clients. From navigation and running sessions to typing and sending, it adds a subtle layer of motion to everyday development."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why Lumina",
      "text": "- **Connected interactions.** Panels, menus, dialogs and message transitions flow together, while light and color bring running sessions to life.\n- **Your own style.** Choose the brand finish, colors, motion intensity and send effect. Each effect can be switched off individually.\n- **Native browser capabilities.** No additional animation framework, with support for system reduced-motion preferences."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why Lumina",
      "text": "Lumina does not change models, requests or message content, delay submission, or block typing, clicking and selection."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install and update",
      "text": "Install DeepSeek Harness first, then search for **`ratel-dsh-lumina`** (author golddream-y) in the plugin store.\n\nYou can also install from the command line:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add @ratel-works/dsh-lumina\n```\n\nReplace `<profile>` with the profile you use: typically `desktop` for the desktop client or `web` for Web / PWA.\n\n**After updating the plugin, fully quit and reopen the client** to load the new code. To update from the command line, run the installation command again."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "Open **Lumina / 流光** in DSH settings. Saved changes apply immediately, without restarting."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "- **Effects and style.** Choose colors, motion intensity and a send effect, or turn individual effects off.\n- **Performance and quality.** Choose **Performance**, **Balanced**, **Quality** or **Ultra**; Balanced is the default. Profiles adjust drawing frequency, resolution and detail independently of motion intensity. Hover or focus a profile button to see its parameters. Frame rates are limits, not guarantees, and depend on your device and display.\n- **Turning motion off.** The master switch restores the original interface. When system reduced motion is enabled, Lumina reduces or disables animations automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "Support",
      "text": "This is a plugin I built for myself, released in the open. The whole point is to make tedious development a little more fun. If you find it useful too, you can buy me a coffee:\n\n- [Afdian](https://afdian.com/a/golddream) — WeChat Pay or Alipay\n- [Ko-fi](https://ko-fi.com/golddream_y) — PayPal, card"
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation and development",
      "text": "- [Changelog](CHANGELOG.md): features, improvements and fixes in each release.\n- [Motion demos](docs/demo/README.md): interaction studies and design prototypes; these are not all shipped client effects.\n- [Implementation status](docs/product/功能实现状态.md): shipped features, verification scope and future work.\n- [Publishing and listing](docs/engineering/发布.md): npm releases and plugin-list submissions.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Local development</summary>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation and development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm test\nnpm run build\n\n</details>"
